			"Message": "chore(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 4 components\n\nSynchronize Common, Mountain, Sky, and Wind submodules with the following changes:\n\n**Features:**\n- Sky: Add LAND_ENABLE_WIND to conditionally skip Wind bootstrap (Atom N2) — introduces environment variable that enables \"Mountain + bare workbench\" integration tests when set to \"false\" at build time. Vite inlines the comparison for tree-shaking, producing the smallest shippable surface where gRPC/Tauri IPC isn't desired. Mirrored into Vite's define config with default \"true\".\n- Wind: Add InstallVsix and Uninstall to ExtensionsService (Atom K5) — implement the contract with methods that accept .vsix path/file:// URI for installation, returning the ILocalExtension envelope from Mountain. Uninstall resolves with true after Mountain removes the install directory and broadcasts the uninstalled event. Refactor all IPC invokes to use the Channel registry instead of free-text string literals for compile-time validation. Prior implementation was a no-op stub returning null.\n\n**Updates:**\n- Common: Minor update\n- Mountain: Minor update\n\nThese changes deliver conditional Wind bootstrapping for minimal builds and enable functional VSIX extension management in the editor.",
			"SHA": "2ab3a64ceb14da69d1557cea9ce17c9c56416411"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T23:01:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "4eb5dad7433ecfac221aaa6e744e7bce1e21d98a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T21:48:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Use static fs imports in StripDanglingSourceMaps\n\nReplace dynamic `await import(\"node:fs/promises\")` calls with top-of-file static bindings in the StripDanglingSourceMaps function. Dynamic imports crash with \"Vite module runner has been closed\" because this runs inside `astro:build:done`, after Vite tears down its ModuleRunner. Also switch to `readdir` with `{ withFileTypes: true }` to get `Dirent[]` instead of `string[]`, enabling type-safe `Entry.name` and `Entry.isDirectory()` checks instead of separate `stat` calls.\n\nThese changes ensure the source map stripping process (Step 11b in CopyVSCode) runs reliably during the build.",
			"SHA": "cba20cb80d0db2723e57aaf06b75711472349593"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T20:58:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 2 components\n\nSynchronize Cocoon and Sky submodules with the following changes:\n\n**Features:**\n- Sky: Add vscode-file and vscode-webview-resource URI schemes to Content Security Policy across all editor entry points (Browser, BrowserProxy, Electron, Mountain, index). These schemes are required to load resources from VS Code platform code copied during the build.\n- Sky: Implement Step 11b in CopyVSCode build process to strip dangling `//# sourceMappingURL=…` comments from copied JS files without sibling .map files. Without this, Safari fetches missing maps, receives 404 HTML, and surfaces a SyntaxError for every such file on page load.\n\nThis coordinated update ensures the editor can properly load VS Code platform resources and eliminates Safari build warnings.",
			"SHA": "85d88e98d7b537625274033a6865d50fdab1fe96"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T18:58:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Inject security.workspace.trust.enabled=false by default\n\nAtom I7: Add logic to AppLifecycle to ensure the VS Code workspace trust system is disabled in User/settings.json. Without this, opening the Land repo as a workspace triggers VS Code's trust gate which marks built-in extensions as `DisabledByTrustRequirement` because they ship under `Element/Sky/Target/Static/Application/extensions/` — inside the repo.\n\nThis writes `\"security.workspace.trust.enabled\": false` only if the key isn't already present. Users can opt back in by editing their User/settings.json.\n\nThis ensures built-in extensions load reliably regardless of which folder the user picks as their workspace.",
			"SHA": "4da3261d6c115399b48925f7767f23efeb291678"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781194547232
}